      "scope": "Settlement-process direction that applies the 8.25% rate declared for 2011-12; it adds a procedure for claims in the pipeline and does not alter the rate."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Each financial-year declaration states the rate for that year only. A later year does not supersede an earlier year; no relationship between yearly declarations is inferred.",
    "Issue date is the date of the EPFO circular, not the date of Central Government approval or the date interest is credited. The approving Ministry letter date is quoted in each circular and is not used as commencement.",
    "The 18 March 2011 circular is typed \"Dated: 17.03.2011\" but carries an 18 MAR 2011 stamp and is cited as dated 18.03.2011 by the 27 April 2011 order; 2011-03-18 is used. The Ministry letter of March 2011 is dated 17 March 2011 as cited in that circular; its own date line is not fully legible.",
    "The 9.5% for 2010-11 is described in the circular as a one-time rate. Interim rates for settling claims before a year's rate is declared appear only in the 2011 documents; this history does not state a general interim-rate rule for later years.",
    "The 2024-25 file labelled _Hi.pdf is the English original of the 31 May 2024 circular for 2023-24; the file without that suffix is its Hindi version. The 2026-27 PDF also encloses the Ministry letter of 17 June 2026 and Finance OM of 8 June 2026 on pages 3-4.",
    "Source PDFs were verified against the issuer mirror on 3 November 2026 because the public site returned 404 for these paths that day; the recorded SHA-256 applies to those mirror files.",
    "Rates are for interest on EPF accumulations. Staff Provident Fund quarterly rates, NPS rates, penal damages under 14B, interest under 7Q, interest on belated crediting, TDS on taxable interest and advances are different matters and are not covered.",
    "Declared rates are not a statement of the tax treatment, of interest credited to an individual account, or of the rate for a year after the latest circular here."
  ]
}
